(1832854, 248592, 44944, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RobMol:</b></div><hr/><i> Hoi Luke. Mooie foto, de schadow komt goed uit en die ribbelige achtergrond geeft een mooi effect. Jammer dat hij als thumbnail niet zo goed tot zijn recht komt. En jammer dat er meerdere hetzelfde idee hadden. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, the idea to take a picture of a feather is not that original as I expected, but I am pleased to see this photo has the highest score on the feather-photos :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by RobMol: Hoi Luke. Mooie foto, de schadow komt goed uit en die ribbelige achtergrond geeft een mooi effect. Jammer dat hij als thumbnail niet zo goed tot zijn recht komt. En jammer dat er meerdere hetzelfde idee hadden.   Yes, the idea to take a picture of a feather is not that original as I expected, but I am pleased to see this photo has the highest score on the feather-photos :-)', '2005-11-02 11:17:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1832919, 248562, 37344, '<td valign="top">My intention was for most of the flower itself to be the background with the details being the forground. I had a hard time cropping it to eliminate the gray corners and keep overall flow that I wanted, so I compromised and left a little bit of gray. Since the gray is just a touch at the corners most people don''t seem to notice it too much.<br/> <br/>But yea, I think it''d be a better shot without the gray corners, regardless of the challenge requirements.</td>', 'My intention was for most of the flower itself to be the background with the details being the forground. I had a hard time cropping it to eliminate the gray corners and keep overall flow that I wanted, so I compromised and left a little bit of gray. Since the gray is just a touch at the corners most people don''t seem to notice it too much. But yea, I think it''d be a better shot without the gray corners, regardless of the challenge requirements.', '2005-11-02 11:39:50.000000', NULL, 0),
