(1834818, 247106, 18552, '<td valign="top">This is sure a furry moth - I''m glad it wasn''t in our house, I hate moths. Looking at your picture gave me such a good idea for light on white, Van - I wish I would have thought of it for the challenge! My white (cream color, actually) didn''t do that well, your furry moth has made me think of a really cool idea with a white mouse - wish I would have thought of it before.</td>', 'This is sure a furry moth - I''m glad it wasn''t in our house, I hate moths. Looking at your picture gave me such a good idea for light on white, Van - I wish I would have thought of it for the challenge! My white (cream color, actually) didn''t do that well, your furry moth has made me think of a really cool idea with a white mouse - wish I would have thought of it before.', '2005-11-02 21:57:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1834922, 249022, 36462, '<td valign="top">Looking at this picture of Snowball makes me sad now.  She went missing on Saturday.  We looked everywhere, checked the animal control shelter, started to make posters, and all that stuff.  She showed up this evening looking like something or someone attacked her.  Her poor face is all swollen and it looks like whatever it was tried to scratch her eyes out.  She''s hurting and it makes me very sad.  I don''t know what the vet can really do, other than maybe give her something for pain and an antibiotic.  I''ve never had to deal with a hurt animal like this before....But we are very happy to know she is alive and back home, and that she will recover fine, thank goodness.<br/>Anyways, just thought I would share Snowball''s story.<br/> <br/>I''m not really very sure what to make of that comment?  *shrug*<br/>Again tho, Thank You all for the comments and the praise!!  It is really appreciated!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-11-02 22:43:11.</i></td>', 'Looking at this picture of Snowball makes me sad now.  She went missing on Saturday.  We looked everywhere, checked the animal control shelter, started to make posters, and all that stuff.  She showed up this evening looking like something or someone attacked her.  Her poor face is all swollen and it looks like whatever it was tried to scratch her eyes out.  She''s hurting and it makes me very sad.  I don''t know what the vet can really do, other than maybe give her something for pain and an antibiotic.  I''ve never had to deal with a hurt animal like this before....But we are very happy to know she is alive and back home, and that she will recover fine, thank goodness.Anyways, just thought I would share Snowball''s story. I''m not really very sure what to make of that comment?  *shrug*Again tho, Thank You all for the comments and the praise!!  It is really appreciated!', '2005-11-02 22:34:26.000000', '2005-11-02 22:43:11.000000', 0),
(1834938, 249207, 28710, '<td valign="top">I really think this is a good interpretation of the challenge. It is a really great looking flower. <br/> <br/>Everyone knows that a flower is not a heavy thing, yet so many people didn''t get the connection to the alternative meaning of light.<br/> <br/>Sad. <br/> <br/>Well done!<br/> <br/>Photographically, the only thing I''d like to see different here is the background paper used to shoot this has a little issue with being lifted or something at the back? There is a slight strangeness about the curvature in the shadows at the back back of the flower.</td>', 'I really think this is a good interpretation of the challenge. It is a really great looking flower.  Everyone knows that a flower is not a heavy thing, yet so many people didn''t get the connection to the alternative meaning of light. Sad.  Well done! Photographically, the only thing I''d like to see different here is the background paper used to shoot this has a little issue with being lifted or something at the back? There is a slight strangeness about the curvature in the shadows at the back back of the flower.', '2005-11-02 22:41:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1834968, 247262, 28710, '<td valign="top">May I make an alternative Title suggestion?<br/> <br/>Light on Whole Wheat - A healthier choice.<br/> <br/>;) Nice idea!<br/> <br/>It looks like the butter is being used to hide the grain of the WW bread. I wonder if perhaps you knocked the saturation up as well just to get the egg yolk up there?<br/> <br/>Did you know you can increase saturation in specific color channels as well (or at least you can in PS)? This is legal in basic editing.<br/> <br/>Check out the tutorial on selective desat using basic editing rules if you want to know what is and is not legal in this technique.</td>', 'May I make an alternative Title suggestion? Light on Whole Wheat - A healthier choice. ;) Nice idea! It looks like the butter is being used to hide the grain of the WW bread. I wonder if perhaps you knocked the saturation up as well just to get the egg yolk up there? Did you know you can increase saturation in specific color channels as well (or at least you can in PS)? This is legal in basic editing. Check out the tutorial on selective desat using basic editing rules if you want to know what is and is not legal in this technique.', '2005-11-02 22:55:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1835008, 248563, 28710, '<td valign="top">There is an excellent expression on this girl''s face. For the challenge, it is a bit difficult though.<br/> <br/>I like this image a lot better for the challenge when I crop to exclude the green background. I''m not so sure when taken on it''s own context though.<br/> <br/>I find the contrasting purple in her shirt and green in the background to be highly distracting. When removed, the attention moves right back where it belongs - in her face. I also removed a slice from the top to counteract and keep the eyes on the top third. <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=252820" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/28710/thumb/252820.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/28710/thumb/252820.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/28710/thumb/252820.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Just an idea.</td>', 'There is an excellent expression on this girl''s face. For the challenge, it is a bit difficult though. I like this image a lot better for the challenge when I crop to exclude the green background. I''m not so sure when taken on it''s own context though. I find the contrasting purple in her shirt and green in the background to be highly distracting. When removed, the attention moves right back where it belongs - in her face. I also removed a slice from the top to counteract and keep the eyes on the top third.    Just an idea.', '2005-11-02 23:10:50.000000', NULL, 0),
